`self.path.replace` is still invisible to the ratchet. `visit_Assign` only binds `ast.Name` targets, and `_resolve` only retypes an attribute when it is exactly `parent`. Given `from pathlib import Path` and `class C:
    def __init__(self, path: Path):
        self.path = path
    def m(self):
        self.path.replace("b")
`, the store resolves to `self.path` rather than `pathlib.Path`, so `visit_Call` does not record `os_replace`. That is the same shape as the call sites this change just rewrote (`tmp.replace(self.path)`, `target.replace(self.path)`), so reintroducing them does not trip the counter.

